 "context": "<div data-type=\"note\" data-has-label=\"true\" id=\"fs-id1169084675730\" class=\"watch-physics\" data-label=\"\">\n<div data-type=\"title\" id=\"7\">Watch Physics: Comparing Celsius and Fahrenheit Temperature Scales</div>\n\n<p id=\"fs-id1169084656701\" class=\" \">This video makes a comparison between the Celsius and Fahrenheit temperature scales.</p>\n<div data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-id1169084672272\" data-alt=\"This tutorial compares Celsius and Fahrenheit.\">\n<div data-type=\"alternatives\" class=\"os-has-iframe os-has-link\">\n<a class=\"os-is-link\" target=\"_window\" href=\"https://www.openstax.org/l/02celfahtemp\">Click to view content</a><iframe width=\"660\" height=\"371.4\" src=\"https://www.openstax.org/l/02celfahtemp\" class=\"os-is-iframe\"><!-- no-selfclose --></iframe>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 613885,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "Watch Physics: Comparing Celsius and Fahrenheit Temperature Scales.\n\nThis video makes a comparison between the Celsius and Fahrenheit temperature scales.\n<iframe src=\"https://www.openstax.org/l/02celfahtemp\"></iframe>",
   "stem_html": "Even without the number labels on the thermometer, you could tell which side is marked Fahrenheit and which is Celsius by how the degree marks are spaced. Why?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1163554,
     "content_html": "The separation between two consecutive divisions on the Fahrenheit scale is greater than a similar separation on the Celsius scale, because each degree Fahrenheit is equal to <span data-math=\"1.8\">1.8</span> degrees Celsius."
    },
    {
     "id": 1163557,
     "content_html": "The separation between two consecutive divisions on the Fahrenheit scale is smaller than the similar separation on the Celsius scale, because each degree Celsius is equal to <span data-math=\"1.8\">1.8</span> degrees Fahrenheit."
    },
    {
     "id": 1163555,
     "content_html": "The separation between two consecutive divisions on the Fahrenheit scale is greater than a similar separation on the Celsius scale, because each degree Fahrenheit is equal to <span data-math=\"3.6\">3.6</span> degrees Celsius."
    },
    {
     "id": 1163556,
     "content_html": "The separation between two consecutive divisions on the Fahrenheit scale is smaller than a similar separation on the Celsius scale, because each degree Celsius is equal to <span data-math=\"3.6\">3.6</span> degrees Fahrenheit."
    }
   ],
